"""ConsistencyValue is one value that the consistency rules compared, together
with the number of records of the entity that hold it.

Consistency rules must match for two records to be allowed to share an entity,
so a record whose identifier contradicts an entity's is not merged into it even
though other rules linked them. These are the values those rules looked at.

Only values that a record actually carries are reported, so the counts say how
many records hold a value, not how many records the entity has."""
type ConsistencyValue @goModel(model: "github.com/tilotech/tilores-plugin-api.ConsistencyValue") {
  """Key names what was compared, e.g. the identifier type."""
  key: String!

  """Value is the compared value itself."""
  value: String!

  """Count is the number of records of the entity that hold this value."""
  count: Int!
}

extend type Entity {
  """List the values that the consistency rules compared, with the number of records holding each of them."""
  consistencyValues: [ConsistencyValue!]!
}
